    "answer": {
      "short": "$3$.",
      "worked": "Since $\\tan\\theta=\\frac43$ and $\\theta$ is in the first quadrant, $\\sin\\theta=\\frac45$ and $\\cos\\theta=\\frac35$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos2\\theta&=\\left(\\frac35\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac45\\right)^2\\\\\\cos2\\theta&=-\\frac7{25}\\\\\\sin2\\theta&=2\\left(\\frac45\\right)\\left(\\frac35\\right)\\\\\\sin2\\theta&=\\frac{24}{25}\\\\3\\cos2\\theta+4\\sin2\\theta&=3\\left(-\\frac7{25}\\right)+4\\left(\\frac{24}{25}\\right)\\\\3\\cos2\\theta+4\\sin2\\theta&=\\frac{75}{25}\\\\3\\cos2\\theta+4\\sin2\\theta&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
